      "body": "This [LinkedIn Pulse article](https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/data-transit-potential-gap-business-gdpr-compliance-paul-rosenthal) does say that sensitive data should be protected (even after using SSL/TLS) in transit, and, based on my own intuition, not doing so can leave a connection vulnerable to man-in-the middle attacks that could trigger a GDPR violation complaint from the affected parties or the EU itself.",
